message: If you use Nav Stack Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below.
title: "Nav Stack Lab: a browser simulator for robot navigation with loop analysis and guided lessons"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: szaf
    name-particle: ""
version: "80"
date-released: 2026-10-31
repository-code: https://github.com/spz0git/nav-stack-lab
url: https://spz0git.github.io/nav-stack-lab/
license: MIT
keywords:
  - robotics
  - navigation
  - localization
  - path planning
  - control
  - simulation
  - education
abstract: >-
  A complete robot navigation stack in one HTML file: localization (dead reckoning, EKF, particle filter, EKF-SLAM),
  perception (occupancy mapping, costmaps, agent tracking), planning (A*, RRT*, Hybrid A*, space-time A*) and control
  (pure pursuit, Stanley, rear-wheel feedback, PID, DWA, MPC) on a simulated differential-drive robot or car, a
  linear loop-analysis view checked against the nonlinear simulator, and guided lessons with companion chapters.
